==============================================================================
R3: mu_g rigidity — scoped confirmation + CROSS-EDGE sharing witness
==============================================================================
(a) edge (4,-2), g=gcd(4,2)=2: critical orbit values (should pair by u->-u):
    sharing pairs (i,j, ratio==-1?): [(0, 3, True), (1, 4, True), (2, 5, True)]
    all sharers same modulus (rotation): True
(b) CROSS-EDGE witness: Lambda = q0 + w^2 u^2 + w u + w/u + w^2/u^2
    w=0.40: u+ = -0.625000 (edge {1,2} fold), u- = -0.625000 (edge {-1,-2} fold)
           u+ * u- = 1.000000000000 ; |L(u+)-L(u-)| = 5.55e-17 ; |u+|/|u-| = 1.000
    w=0.15: u+ = -3.000000 (edge {1,2} fold), u- = -0.333333 (edge {-1,-2} fold)
           u+ * u- = 1.000000000000 ; |L(u+)-L(u-)| = 1.67e-16 ; |u+|/|u-| = 9.000
    w=0.05: u+ = -9.898979 (edge {1,2} fold), u- = -0.101021 (edge {-1,-2} fold)
           u+ * u- = 1.000000000000 ; |L(u+)-L(u-)| = 0.00e+00 ; |u+|/|u-| = 97.990
    => EXACT value sharing between folds on DIFFERENT edges, related by
       INVERSION u -> 1/u (moduli differ: NOT a mu_g rotation).
       'Deleted hijacked stacks are symmetry stacks (mu_g)' is proved ONLY
       for events on ONE two-term edge; cross-edge sharing is real.

